<p><strong>Figure 6.</strong> Angular magniﬁcation. The image P of a point P is shown together with the angles which a ray makes with these points.</p>

<h5 id="3-the-entrance-and-exit-pupils">3. The entrance and exit pupils</h5>
<p><strong><em>The entrance and exit pupils</em></strong> of an optical system are important in limiting its resolution and light-gathering power.</p>

<p><strong>Entrance pupil</strong>: The image of that aperture, formed by the optical system which precedes it, which subtends the smallest angle at the object. The <strong>‘aperture stop’</strong> is the physical aperture whose image forms the entrance pupil.</p>

<p><strong>Exit pupil</strong>: The image of the entrance pupil formed by the whole system.</p>

